    {
      "id": "a1_u08_l01",
      "level": "A1",
      "unit": 8,
      "title": "Quelle heure est-il ?",
      "description": "Ask for and tell the time, from full hours to quarter to.",
      "estimatedMinutes": 12,
      "sections": [
        {
          "type": "learn",
          "title": "Learn",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "heading": "Asking and telling the time",
              "body": "To ask the time, say \"Quelle heure est-il ?\" (What time is it?). The answer always starts with \"il est\", even though there is no \"he\" involved — it is just how French tells the time.",
              "examples": [
                { "french": "Quelle heure est-il ?", "english": "What time is it?" },
                { "french": "Il est trois heures.", "english": "It is three o'clock." },
                { "french": "Il est une heure.", "english": "It is one o'clock." },
                { "french": "Il est midi.", "english": "It is noon." },
                { "french": "Il est dix heures.", "english": "It is ten o'clock." },
                { "french": "Il est minuit, bonne nuit !", "english": "It is midnight, good night!" }
              ],
              "tip": "For 12 o'clock, French has two special words: \"midi\" (noon) and \"minuit\" (midnight) — no \"heures\" needed."
            },
            {
              "heading": "Half past and quarters",
              "body": "Add \"et quart\" for quarter past, \"et demie\" for half past, and \"moins le quart\" for quarter to the next hour. So 2:45 is \"trois heures moins le quart\" — quarter to three.",
              "examples": [
                { "french": "Il est quatre heures et quart.", "english": "It is quarter past four." },
                { "french": "Il est quatre heures et demie.", "english": "It is half past four." },
                { "french": "Il est cinq heures moins le quart.", "english": "It is quarter to five." },
                { "french": "Il est une heure et demie.", "english": "It is half past one." },
                { "french": "Il est neuf heures et quart.", "english": "It is quarter past nine." }
              ],
              "tip": "After \"midi\" and \"minuit\", write \"et demi\" without the final e: \"midi et demi\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
