    {
      "id": "a1_u08_l02",
      "level": "A1",
      "unit": 8,
      "title": "Les jours et les mois",
      "description": "Learn the days of the week, the months, and yesterday, today and tomorrow.",
      "estimatedMinutes": 12,
      "sections": [
        {
          "type": "learn",
          "title": "Learn",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "heading": "The days of the week",
              "body": "The French week starts on Monday: lundi, mardi, mercredi, jeudi, vendredi, samedi, dimanche. Days are written with a small letter, never a capital.",
              "examples": [
                { "french": "Aujourd'hui, c'est lundi.", "english": "Today is Monday." },
                { "french": "Nous sommes jeudi.", "english": "It is Thursday.", "note": "literally: we are Thursday" },
                { "french": "Samedi et dimanche, c'est le week-end !", "english": "Saturday and Sunday — it's the weekend!" },
                { "french": "Vendredi soir, je vais au cinéma.", "english": "On Friday evening, I go to the cinema." },
                { "french": "On est mercredi aujourd'hui.", "english": "It's Wednesday today.", "note": "informal" }
              ],
              "tip": "\"On est mardi\" is a very common, informal way to say \"it's Tuesday\"."
            },
            {
              "heading": "The months",
              "body": "The twelve months are: janvier, février, mars, avril, mai, juin, juillet, août, septembre, octobre, novembre, décembre. Use \"en\" to say in which month something happens.",
              "examples": [
                { "french": "Mon anniversaire est en juin.", "english": "My birthday is in June." },
                { "french": "En août, je suis en vacances.", "english": "In August, I am on holiday." },
                { "french": "En décembre, c'est Noël.", "english": "In December, it's Christmas." },
                { "french": "Le mois de mai est très joli.", "english": "The month of May is very pretty." }
              ],
              "tip": "Like the days, months never take a capital letter in French."
            },
            {
              "heading": "Yesterday, today, tomorrow",
              "body": "Three little words you will use every day: \"hier\" (yesterday), \"aujourd'hui\" (today) and \"demain\" (tomorrow).",
              "examples": [
                { "french": "Hier, c'était dimanche.", "english": "Yesterday was Sunday." },
                { "french": "Aujourd'hui, c'est lundi.", "english": "Today is Monday." },
                { "french": "Demain, c'est mardi.", "english": "Tomorrow is Tuesday." },
                { "french": "Demain, je ne travaille pas.", "english": "Tomorrow, I am not working." }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "vocabulary",
          "title": "Vocabulary",
          "items": [
